        "message": "Here are three practical ways to approach this while you depend on them for rent: 1. **Address the stability fear with data.** Parents who push for stability often assume creative fields mean erratic freelance income. Showing them concrete examples—entry-level salaries, benefits, and career paths for in-house graphic design, production, or UI/UX roles—can directly target what they're nervous about. 2. **Use a bridge strategy.** You could take a steady job—either an entry-level corporate design role or a standard job that pays the bills—while building your target design portfolio on the side. This keeps rent covered and lowers conflict while you build momentum. 3. **Set a timeline for paying your own rent.** Figure out the exact monthly income and savings buffer you need to cover your own housing. Once you have a clear financial target, you can work toward removing the leverage they currently have over your career choices. Which of those angles feels most workable for you right now?",
